// Source: expressions.md "Capture in string interpolation": `(expr)$` pastes
// the value of `expr`, so `()$` and `( )$` have nothing to paste, in an
// ordinary or raw string and in a function expression. Upstream emits
// `cpp2::to_string()`, which does not compile.
// expect-error: (9,18): error: a string interpolation '(...)$' needs an expression
// expect-error: (10,31): error: a string interpolation '(...)$' needs an expression
// expect-error: (11,18): error: a string interpolation '(...)$' needs an expression
main: () = {
    std::cout << "cost ()$ \n";
    l := :() -> std::string = "( )$";
    std::cout << $R"(x ()$)" << l();
}
